1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,552
A bus pulls away from a stop.

2
00:00:02,552 --> 00:00:04,298
A ball rolls to a halt.

3
00:00:04,298 --> 00:00:05,934
A lift starts to rise.

4
00:00:06,334 --> 00:00:07,754
Three different things.

5
00:00:07,754 --> 00:00:10,431
But in all three, the
velocity is changing.

6
00:00:10,881 --> 00:00:15,006
Outside Diya's college, an ambulance
sets off from the gate, its siren

7
00:00:15,006 --> 00:00:15,906
on.

8
00:00:15,785 --> 00:00:17,798
Its speed climbs every second.

9
00:00:17,798 --> 00:00:21,990
But how fast is the speed itself
climbing, at one exact instant?

10
00:00:22,490 --> 00:00:24,797
By the end of this video,
you will measure it.

11
00:00:25,447 --> 00:00:27,107
So what is acceleration?

12
00:00:27,457 --> 00:00:30,725
Acceleration is how fast
the velocity changes.

13
00:00:30,725 --> 00:00:34,455
The change in velocity,
divided by the time taken.

14
00:00:34,855 --> 00:00:37,570
Its SI unit is metres per second squared.

15
00:00:37,970 --> 00:00:42,404
Two metres per second squared means
the velocity grows by two metres per

16
00:00:42,404 --> 00:00:43,985
second, every second.

17
00:00:44,635 --> 00:00:47,540
Let's watch the ambulance
on our motion notebook.

18
00:00:47,890 --> 00:00:49,461
It starts from rest.

19
00:00:49,461 --> 00:00:54,520
Its velocity is v equals four t, minus
a quarter t squared, in metres per

20
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:55,420
second.

21
00:00:55,616 --> 00:00:57,676
Watch the velocity arrow grow.

22
00:00:57,676 --> 00:00:59,998
Fast at first, then more slowly.

23
00:01:00,398 --> 00:01:03,265
The velocity time graph
curves and flattens out.

24
00:01:03,665 --> 00:01:05,153
Slow motion replay.

25
00:01:05,153 --> 00:01:07,483
Freeze at t equals two seconds.

26
00:01:07,983 --> 00:01:10,629
The velocity is seven metres per second.

27
00:01:10,629 --> 00:01:13,384
But how fast is it changing, right now?

28
00:01:14,034 --> 00:01:15,226
Try an average.

29
00:01:15,226 --> 00:01:19,441
From two seconds to six seconds,
v goes from seven to fifteen.

30
00:01:19,441 --> 00:01:20,684
Eight over four.

31
00:01:20,684 --> 00:01:22,756
Two metres per second squared.

32
00:01:23,206 --> 00:01:25,435
Shrink the gap to two seconds.

33
00:01:25,435 --> 00:01:26,628
Five over two.

34
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:27,874
Two point five.

35
00:01:28,324 --> 00:01:29,348
One second.

36
00:01:29,348 --> 00:01:31,694
Two point seven five over one.

37
00:01:31,694 --> 00:01:33,407
Two point seven five.

38
00:01:33,857 --> 00:01:35,390
A tenth of a second.

39
00:01:35,390 --> 00:01:37,220
Two point nine seven five.

40
00:01:37,670 --> 00:01:39,395
A hundredth of a second.

41
00:01:39,395 --> 00:01:41,525
Two point nine nine seven five.

42
00:01:41,525 --> 00:01:43,605
The answers close in on three.

43
00:01:44,055 --> 00:01:46,983
On the graph, the chord
turns into the tangent.

44
00:01:46,983 --> 00:01:48,284
Its slope is three.

45
00:01:48,934 --> 00:01:51,759
Let's write this as a
rule, one step at a time.

46
00:01:52,109 --> 00:01:53,061
Step one.

47
00:01:53,061 --> 00:01:57,593
Average acceleration, a bar,
equals delta v over delta t.

48
00:01:58,343 --> 00:01:59,270
Step two.

49
00:01:59,270 --> 00:02:01,768
Let delta t shrink towards zero.

50
00:02:01,768 --> 00:02:06,844
The acceleration at an instant is
the limit of delta v over delta t.

51
00:02:07,594 --> 00:02:08,560
Step three.

52
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:11,122
This limit is written d v by d t.

53
00:02:11,122 --> 00:02:14,744
The slope of the tangent
on the velocity time graph.

54
00:02:15,494 --> 00:02:16,418
Step four.

55
00:02:16,418 --> 00:02:19,511
Here, d v by d t is four minus half t.

56
00:02:19,511 --> 00:02:21,860
At two seconds, that is three.

57
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:23,443
Just like our table.

58
00:02:24,193 --> 00:02:25,274
Remember this.

59
00:02:25,274 --> 00:02:28,234
Velocity is the slope
of the position graph.

60
00:02:28,234 --> 00:02:31,396
Acceleration is the slope
of the velocity graph.

61
00:02:32,096 --> 00:02:33,168
Side by side.

62
00:02:33,168 --> 00:02:37,653
When velocity and acceleration point
the same way, the speed goes up.

63
00:02:38,053 --> 00:02:41,186
When they point opposite
ways, the speed goes down.

64
00:02:41,786 --> 00:02:42,874
Now you try.

65
00:02:42,874 --> 00:02:45,051
A ball is thrown straight up.

66
00:02:45,051 --> 00:02:47,936
At the very top, its velocity is zero.

67
00:02:47,936 --> 00:02:50,430
Is its acceleration zero there too?

68
00:02:50,430 --> 00:02:51,783
Pause and decide.

69
00:02:54,983 --> 00:02:55,883
No!

70
00:02:55,477 --> 00:03:00,560
Gravity still pulls it down at nine
point eight metres per second squared.

71
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:03,548
The velocity is zero for only an instant.

72
00:03:04,198 --> 00:03:05,387
One more thing.

73
00:03:05,387 --> 00:03:08,703
A negative sign does not
always mean slowing down.

74
00:03:09,053 --> 00:03:13,191
The sign only tells the direction,
compared with the positive direction

75
00:03:13,191 --> 00:03:14,091
we chose.

76
00:03:14,369 --> 00:03:19,259
An ambulance driving left and speeding
up has negative velocity and negative

77
00:03:19,259 --> 00:03:20,286
acceleration.

78
00:03:20,686 --> 00:03:21,628
Your turn.

79
00:03:21,628 --> 00:03:26,344
Velocity minus ten metres per second,
acceleration minus two metres per

80
00:03:26,344 --> 00:03:27,556
second squared.

81
00:03:27,556 --> 00:03:29,665
Speeding up or slowing down?

82
00:03:29,665 --> 00:03:30,996
Pause and think.

83
00:03:34,196 --> 00:03:35,151
Speeding up!

84
00:03:35,151 --> 00:03:36,875
Both point the same way.

85
00:03:36,875 --> 00:03:38,539
Signs match, speed up.

86
00:03:38,539 --> 00:03:40,302
Signs differ, slow down.

87
00:03:40,952 --> 00:03:42,688
Now, one worked example.

88
00:03:43,038 --> 00:03:46,777
The ambulance has v equals
three t squared plus two t.

89
00:03:46,777 --> 00:03:51,614
Find the average acceleration in the
first two seconds, and the acceleration

90
00:03:51,614 --> 00:03:52,836
at two seconds.

91
00:03:53,336 --> 00:03:55,657
At t equals zero, v is zero.

92
00:03:55,657 --> 00:03:58,695
At t equals two, v is twelve plus four.

93
00:03:58,695 --> 00:04:00,610
Sixteen metres per second.

94
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:04,071
Average acceleration is sixteen over two.

95
00:04:04,071 --> 00:04:06,262
Eight metres per second squared.

96
00:04:07,012 --> 00:04:09,550
For the instant, find d v by d t.

97
00:04:09,550 --> 00:04:11,358
a equals six t plus two.

98
00:04:12,108 --> 00:04:15,670
At two seconds, a is fourteen
metres per second squared.

99
00:04:15,670 --> 00:04:17,371
Almost double the average.

100
00:04:18,021 --> 00:04:19,486
Now, the exam trap.

101
00:04:19,836 --> 00:04:24,081
Many students think that zero
velocity means zero acceleration.

102
00:04:24,481 --> 00:04:25,381
Not true.

103
00:04:25,345 --> 00:04:30,137
At the top of a throw, v is zero,
but a is still g, downwards.

104
00:04:30,137 --> 00:04:32,780
Acceleration depends on how v changes.

105
00:04:33,430 --> 00:04:34,992
Where is this asked?

106
00:04:34,992 --> 00:04:40,276
Given v as a function of t, find the
average acceleration, and the acceleration

107
00:04:40,276 --> 00:04:41,513
at one instant.

108
00:04:42,113 --> 00:04:43,352
Exam level now.

109
00:04:43,352 --> 00:04:46,439
v equals t squared
minus four t plus three.

110
00:04:46,439 --> 00:04:51,395
Find the average acceleration from zero
to four seconds, and the acceleration

111
00:04:51,395 --> 00:04:52,959
when it first stops.

112
00:04:52,959 --> 00:04:54,251
Pause and solve.

113
00:04:59,651 --> 00:05:00,979
The answer is B.

114
00:05:00,979 --> 00:05:04,202
Zero, and minus two
metres per second squared.

115
00:05:04,702 --> 00:05:06,300
v at zero is three.

116
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:09,910
v at four is sixteen,
minus sixteen, plus three.

117
00:05:09,910 --> 00:05:10,890
Also three.

118
00:05:10,890 --> 00:05:13,457
So the average acceleration is zero.

119
00:05:13,957 --> 00:05:17,831
It first stops when v is
zero, at t equals one second.

120
00:05:17,831 --> 00:05:19,794
a equals two t minus four.

121
00:05:19,794 --> 00:05:22,271
Minus two metres per second squared.

122
00:05:22,871 --> 00:05:24,335
Here is your recap.

123
00:05:24,335 --> 00:05:25,840
Screenshot this card.

124
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:31,876
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

125
00:05:32,276 --> 00:05:33,176
One.

126
00:05:32,798 --> 00:05:36,213
Can a body have zero velocity
and still accelerate?

127
00:05:37,113 --> 00:05:38,013
Two.

128
00:05:37,608 --> 00:05:41,118
What does the slope of a
velocity time graph tell you?

129
00:05:42,018 --> 00:05:42,918
Three.

130
00:05:42,690 --> 00:05:47,371
With velocity negative and acceleration
positive, is the body speeding

131
00:05:47,371 --> 00:05:48,956
up or slowing down?

132
00:05:50,056 --> 00:05:53,453
Next time: same change
every second, or not?

133
00:05:53,453 --> 00:05:55,732
Uniform and non uniform motion.
